From: Oasis <info@oasis.net>
Subject: [PATCH] configure: allow recipe-managed Python and Meson

Yocto's native Python sysconfig uses the staged prefix even inside a venv.
QEMU therefore mistakes staged packages for venv-local packages and tries
to reinstall them with pip. Ubuntu's repacked source has no fallback wheels.

Let these private native recipes supply Python and Meson directly, following
OE-Core's fixedmeson/no-pip approach while retaining the selected interpreter.
The 8.2 recipe uses meson-native; 10.1 extracts its bundled wheels locally.
Fail any later request to install optional Python dependencies in this mode.
The normal upstream bootstrap remains available outside the recipes.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [OE-specific native build integration]

diff --git a/configure b/configure
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -938,6 +938,13 @@
 echo "python determined to be '$python'"
 echo "python version: $($python --version)"
 
+# Private native recipes provide all build-time Python dependencies offline.
+if test -n "$OASIS_MESON"; then
+    python="$python -B"
+    mkvenv=false
+    meson="$OASIS_MESON"
+else
+
 python="$($python -B "${source_path}/python/scripts/mkvenv.py" create pyvenv)"
 if test "$?" -ne 0 ; then
     error_exit "python venv creation failed"
@@ -961,6 +968,7 @@
 # *exclusively*.
 
 meson="$(cd pyvenv/bin; pwd)/meson"
+fi
 
 # Conditionally ensure Sphinx is installed.
 
